    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d317-a5">

                <pb facs="0624" n="564" xml:id="pg564"/>

                <opener><dateline rendition="#center">[From the Diario Oficial, City of
                            <placeName>Mexico</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1868-06-10">June 10,
                    1868</date>.—Translation.]</dateline></opener>
                <head>Tamaulipas.</head>
                <p>An American, Dr. Huchinson, tried to smuggle out from Matamoras to Brownsville a
                    hundred ounces (pieces of sixteen dollars) of gold; the inspector discovered the
                    fraud and the ounces were confiscated.</p>
                <p>It appears that the American consul protested and asked from the custom-house
                    authorities the return of the money. The Observador says that the protest is
                    inopportune and unfounded, and recommends energetic proceedings.</p>
                <p>The papers of Brownsville have raised a great cry about this affair, and pretend
                    that the American government will intervene.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
